     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Dear Ben,</div><div><br></div><div>I am reposting this question with RStanarm in the title, as suggested by Bob. Thanks for any guidance!</div><div><br></div><div>------------</div><div>I am trying to compute the SD and the 95% credible intervals around the SD for the random/group effects for each variable starting from rstanarm summaries. </div><div><br></div><div>My model formula is of the form: <span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\"> formula &lt;- &quot;response ~ var1_scaled + ... + var17_scaled + (</span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">var1_scaled + ... + var17_scaled</span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">|donor)&quot;</span></div><div><br></div><div>I tried computing the SD from the posterior summaries but my answer does not match up with the output of the print() function.</div><div><br></div><div>For example: print(modelresults) gives me the following output</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\">Error terms:</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\"> Groups Name            Std.Dev. Corr                                                                                                 </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\"> donor  (Intercept)    0.023977                                                                                                      </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\">        var1_scaled    0.023524  0.00                                                                                                </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\">        var2_scaled    0.023307  0.00  0.00                                                                                          </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\">        var3_scaled    0.022573  0.00  0.00  0.00        