     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Thursday, June 2, 2016 at 12:48:15 AM UTC-4, Jyoti Shankar wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I tried computing the SD from the posterior summaries but my answer does not match up with the output of the print() function.</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>The output of the print() function for the group-level covariance is not &quot;correct&quot;. In particular, the reported standard deviations are the square roots of the posterior means of the variances rather than the posterior means of the square roots of the variances. We do not actually store what would be needed to directly calculate stuff like this directly, so it is conceptually better to do what you did ...<br>  <br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>However, if I calculate the standard deviations of these terms from the posterior samples as follows:<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">##########</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\"># extract posterior samples</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>mat </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">as</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">modelresults</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\"># get the random effect columns</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>group_cols </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> grep</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;^b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> colnames</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mat</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> value </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> T</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>group_posteriors </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> mat</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> group_cols</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\"># example variable slope term: b[var1_scaled donor:donor1]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>variable_names </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> unique</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">gsub</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;b\\\\[(.*)\\\\s.*&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;\\\\1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> colnames</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">group_posteriors</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)))</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\"># for each variable, compute its SD at each MCMC iteration</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>var_group_summary </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> sapply</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">variable_names</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">function</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">vname</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">){</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>    var_group_posteriors </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> group_posteriors</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> grep</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">vname</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> colnames</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">group_posteriors</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> value </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> T</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>    group_sd </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> sapply</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">nrow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">var_group_posteriors</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">function</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">crow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">){</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">out</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> sd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">var_group_posteriors</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">crow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">])</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">return</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">out</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">})</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>    group_summary </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mean </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">group_sd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> quantile</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> group_sd</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> probs </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.025</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.975</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)))</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">return</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">group_summary</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">})</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">return</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">var_group_summary</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">##########</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></code></div><div></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div> <br>However, the standard deviation of some unknown across groups at each MCMC iteration could be a noisy estimate if the number of levels of that grouping variable is small.<br><br>Ben<br><br></div></div>"
